			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Restructure project layout to flat 'Archive' directory\n\nThis commit flattens the Wind project's directory structure by relocating all source files from the nested `Source/Archive/*` path to the top-level `Archive/*` directory.\n\nThis architectural cleanup removes an unnecessary layer of nesting from the monorepo structure, simplifying the module resolution and import paths for the Wind service layer. The move encompasses the entire `Application` domain (including Define, Implement, Problem, and Convert files), as well as `Integration`, `Platform`, `TypeConverter`, `Bridge`, and `Effect` utilities.\n\nAdditionally, the TypeScript build output has been updated to reflect these changes, regenerating declaration files and source maps for the affected modules and the build cache (`tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`).",
			"SHA": "17c7dc37050b9e16cb566a10d5d8b90104a0b325"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-31T20:47:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				621,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Enforce type-only exports for Effect service interfaces\n\nThis commit updates the barrel file `Source/Effect/index.ts` to strictly re-export service interfaces and associated types using the `export type` syntax.\n\nIn the Effect-TS architecture utilized by Wind, it is critical to distinguish between the structural definition of a service (the interface) and its runtime implementation (the tag). By migrating exports like `IPCService` and `MountainService` to `export type`, we prevent accidental runtime usage of these interfaces and ensure cleaner type-only imports for consumers within the Wind service layer and Sky UI components.\n\nThis refactoring standardizes the export pattern across all core services: IPC, Sandbox, Configuration, Telemetry, and Mountain.",
			"SHA": "cf79bc0edee90aa77e5de559e9a658264f27385f"
		},
